user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hacst/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hacst/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hacst/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hacst/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hacst/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hacst/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hacst/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2021-07-12T13:30:14Z","updated_at":"2021-07-12T13:53:13Z","body":"Some further analysis: Adding the custom exporter adds an additional `SimpleSpanProcessor` for each exporter:\r\nhttps://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/blob/ec2c72d7f1c5990be14ebbea140afb0ddc90d196/extensions/opentelemetry/opentelemetry/runtime/src/main/java/io/quarkus/opentelemetry/runtime/tracing/TracerRecorder.java#L79\r\n\r\nDue to that OTEL creates a `MultiSpanProcessor`\r\nhttps://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-java/blob/ae4bb364cdf6cdae583f07209ce514674c98fdbd/sdk/trace/src/main/java/io/opentelemetry/sdk/trace/SpanProcessor.java#L45-L48\r\nduring construction that type calls `isStartRequired` on the processors:\r\nhttps://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-java/blob/ae4bb364cdf6cdae583f07209ce514674c98fdbd/sdk/trace/src/main/java/io/opentelemetry/sdk/trace/MultiSpanProcessor.java#L87\r\nThis operation on `LateBoundBatchSpanProcessor` requires the delegate. This violates the assumption that creation of the delegate can be omitted during static initialization.\r\n\r\n`isStartRequired` returns false after emitting the warning. I assume this prevents the `MultiSpanProcessor` from starting the jaeger exporter later on which would explain it not working.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/quarkusio/quarkus/issues/comments/878281280/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confus